{
	title: 'SAVE_SECRET tool prompts user and writes env secrets on the host',
	spec: 'Agent tool SAVE_SECRET /* <purpose> */ { file, name } (enableIf: $session_interactive) prompts the user with a hidden secret form (skip: true) and writes NAME=value atomically (temp file + rename) to the env file on the host. New files are created with mode 0600; existing files preserve their permissions. The secret value travels only from client to host and never enters history, events, logs, or tool results; the agent receives only saved, canceled (Escape or empty input), or an error. Replaces an existing NAME= value matched at start of file or after CR/LF, or appends NAME=value (matching CRLF if present, otherwise LF). Warns in the question text ("This replaces the current value.") when the variable already exists. Validates name as [A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*, checks writability before prompting, and refuses values containing CR/LF or NUL. Tool card titles use the /* purpose */ comment or fall back to "Save <NAME> to <file>". System prompt Other tools lists the one-line call example and description; HELP SAVE_SECRET documents full usage.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'Simplified 2026-11-25 (user): dropped git/gitignore/symlink checks, gated on enableIf: $session_interactive (reverting Other tools stripPurpose workaround), preserved permissions on existing files (0600 for new files), simplified env editing to a line-start NAME= regex with CRLF detection, widened names to [A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*, and added writability checks before prompting.'
